  "content": {
    "text": "4 days ago\nThe SOX chip sector tracker is seeing a near-unanimous surge to a weekly gain\nDon't blame the chip sector for the weakness in the tech sector this week. The PHLX Semiconductor Index is surging 3.6% on the day, with 29 of 30 components gaining ground, and is now up 3.5% on the week.\nMeanwhile, the State Street Technology Select Sector SPDR ETF is trading up 1.3% on the day, but is still down 0.8% this week, after closing Wednesday in correction territory.\nSoftware has more to do with the tech weakness, as the iShares Expanded Tech-Software ETF is losing 1.4% on Thursday -- thanks, Oracle -- and has dropped 5.8% this week.",
